| skill list, goal, todo, todo list, ast foo --in . | 0 | 0 |

Output was identical before and after in every row. The scripts/workflows check you asked for (grep -rnE "yoyo (skill\|goal\|todo\|ast)\b" scripts/ .github/) found 0 hits, so nothing in this repo's own loop relies on the old exit code.

What changed, in 3 source files:
• `skill` (src/commands_skill.rs): the unknown-subcommand branch returns 2. This file wasn't in the task's list; it's the one extra file the constraints allowed.
• `goal` (src/commands_goal.rs): a new goal_subcommand_is_unknown check. The /goal handler and the shell's exit code both use it, so the message and the exit code can't disagree. A test checks it against every real verb.
• `todo` and `ast` (src/dispatch_sub.rs): todo exits 2 when the verb isn't a known one; bare todo still lists and exits 0. ast exits 2 whenever the parser the command already uses rejects the input. "ast-grep not installed" still exits 0, since that isn't a usage error.

Things to know:
• `ast` covers more than bare `ast`. Every input its parser rejects now exits 2, including --lang with no value and a bare path like ast $X.unwrap() src/.
• I edited one existing test. It checked that ast $X.unwrap() src/ gets routed, but that input now exits 2 mid-test, which would kill the test run. That case now uses the --in src/ form. The bare-path form's exit 2 is checked in the new test.
• The file-size limit moved. In tests/module_size.rs, src/dispatch_sub.rs goes from 2336 to 2457 lines. That's 56 lines of earlier unrecorded growth plus this change; the reason is in the comment and the commit.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md now lists the new exit codes.

Still exiting 0 (listed in the commit body): usage errors that aren't unknown verbs (bare skill show, skill init, skill install, and todo list extra). Also the rest of #982 that this task didn't cover: the undo failure paths, setup/version/def (not probed), bare run (by decision), and the 1-vs-2 disagreement on tree. I didn't post a #982 comment, because the task only asked for one if the fixes didn't fit in 3 files.
